; BALANCES row order (#2409): bean-query orders rows by account_sortkey,
; account type first (Assets, Liabilities, Equity, Income, Expenses), then
; name. Every account type is present, each in a transaction that touches
; Assets (the corpus query is `BALANCES FROM has_account('Assets')`), so a
; plain name order (Assets, Equity, Expenses, Income, Liabilities) differs.

2024-01-01 open Assets:Bank:Checking USD
2024-01-01 open Assets:Cash USD
2024-01-01 open Liabilities:CreditCard USD
2024-01-01 open Liabilities:Loan USD
2024-01-01 open Equity:Opening-Balances USD
2024-01-01 open Income:Salary USD
2024-01-01 open Income:Interest USD
2024-01-01 open Expenses:Food USD
2024-01-01 open Expenses:Rent USD

2024-01-02 * "Opening balance"
  Assets:Bank:Checking   1000.00 USD
  Equity:Opening-Balances

2024-01-15 * "Payroll"
  Assets:Bank:Checking   3000.00 USD
  Income:Salary

2024-01-20 * "Interest"
  Assets:Bank:Checking      1.25 USD
  Income:Interest

2024-02-01 * "Rent"
  Expenses:Rent          1500.00 USD
  Assets:Bank:Checking

2024-02-03 * "Groceries on the card"
  Expenses:Food            85.40 USD
  Liabilities:CreditCard

2024-02-10 * "Pay the card"
  Liabilities:CreditCard   85.40 USD
  Assets:Bank:Checking

2024-02-12 * "Borrow"
  Assets:Cash             200.00 USD
  Liabilities:Loan

2024-02-14 * "Lunch"
  Expenses:Food            12.00 USD
  Assets:Cash
